DIAGNOSTIC_INTERPRETATION_2026-09-23
- Minimal AppDriver with clean Windows locale and explicit Chrome timed out waiting for Page.navigate after Shiny reported listening; this reproduces startup failure without the full test suite.
- Independent Chromote data: navigation and DOM read succeeded on Chrome/153.0.8010.53. Independent warm Shiny: HTTP 200 after 40.647 s; Page.navigate succeeded in 4.359 s.
- AppDriver began Page.navigate approximately 35.8 s after Shiny startup and hit Chromote's 10.0 s command timeout. Cold-page timing is a plausible explanation, not a demonstrated root cause. Shiny process announcing Listening does not prove first-page completion.
- Immediate DOM evaluation in the warm Shiny probe returned document.body null; Page.navigate itself succeeded. The probe did not wait for DOM readiness, so it does not establish complete UI load.
- No application code, dependency, or timeout was changed. Four original suite error traces remained pending when this note was written.
